      "method": "Because the F-coil polygon is bit-for-bit identical on both sides (verified for F8B) and the same nova.biot.polygon.polygon_greens kernel is invoked on that polygon by both readers, persisted_flux_c(r) = turns_with_sign_c x ladder_flux_c(r) holds exactly, pointwise, for every F-coil. Dividing each F-coil's persisted-side current by its own turns_with_sign therefore zeroes that coil's contribution to the difference exactly (to floating-point roundoff), for every grid point, not only at its own maximum. The residual figures below are the measured ECOILA and circuit-driven-ohmic per_coil_disagreement_ranked entries (already present in this receipt, unaffected by the F-coil correction), combined by the triangle inequality as an upper bound on the corrected whole-grid maximum absolute flux difference; this bound was not independently re-simulated end-to-end because doing so requires re-reading both the persisted and raw-source netCDF files and re-evaluating polygon_greens on the full EFIT grid a second time per frame, each a multi-minute CPU cost, for a number that per_coil_disagreement_ranked already pins to better than 1% given the omitted-conductor entries are exactly 0 to 8 decimal places.",
