    "summary": "The 18 F-coils are double-counted in the persisted machine description: each is authored as a single pf_active element whose polygon outline is bit-for-bit the same bulk winding-pack cross-section the row-derived challenge description uses (verified directly for F8B: identical four vertices, same winding order, only the starting vertex differs), yet the persisted element also carries turns_with_sign = 58 or 55 (the physical turn count). The row-derived description already treats the shipped F-coil channel as total ampere-turns applied to that same bulk polygon with no turns multiplier (TurnConvention.applied_multiplier = 1.0, \"recorded F-coil channel already contains total ampere-turns\"). Feeding that same total-ampere-turns current through active_coil_response_from_imas's convention (response = turns_with_sign x polygon_greens(element)) multiplies by the turn count a second time, so persisted_flux_c(r) = turns_with_sign_c x ladder_flux_c(r) exactly, pointwise, for every F-coil -- consistent with the measured per_coil_disagreement_ranked pattern (nonzero only for the 18 F-coils, scaling with each coil's own turns_with_sign, and exactly 0 for ECOILA and the five circuit-driven ohmic channels, which are authored as genuine one-turn-per-element sub-loops on both sides).",
    "unit_convention_each_side_uses": {
      "persisted_description (docs/figures/diiid-forward-onboarding/ids-set/diiid_machine_description.nc, read through nova.imas.diiid_description.active_coil_response_from_imas)": "coil current is expected to be per-turn amps (A); response = turns_with_sign x polygon_greens(element), summed over elements -- correct for ECOILA/ECOILB/E567*/E89* (each authored as N genuine one-turn elements, turns_with_sign = 1 apiece) but wrong for the 18 F-coils, which reuse the bulk (total-ampere-turn) polygon under this per-turn convention",
      "row_derived_challenge_description (what the ladder drives its F-coil response from, nova.imas.diiid_description._description_from_row / dataset_machine_description)": "coil current = total ampere-turns (A.turn); one bulk winding-pack polygon per coil; response = polygon_greens(bulk polygon) with no turns multiplier applied (TurnConvention.applied_multiplier = 1.0 for every F-coil and for ECOILA)"
    },
    "verdict": "Dividing the F-coil currents by their turns_with_sign does NOT bring the comparison to the 1e-12 roundoff bound. It exactly removes the F-coil contribution (confirmed analytically), leaving a residual of about 10.7-11.4% of the ladder's peak flux on the two scored frames, entirely attributable to ECOILA: the row-derived description represents ECOILA as one bulk rectangular polygon carrying the total ampere-turns directly, while the persisted description represents it as 48 discrete one-turn ring elements; both apply the correct (non-double-counted) turns convention, so this is a separate, smaller geometric-discretization difference rather than a unit-convention defect, and is recorded as a follow-on rather than fixed here."
